🔁 CONVERTING LOOPS → STREAMS (SYSTEMATIC)
🔑 Golden rule (read first)
First write / understand the loop → then convert to stream
Never think in streams first.

1️⃣ Simple iteration (forEach)
Loop
for (int x : list) {
    System.out.println(x);
}

Stream
list.stream().forEach(System.out::println);

🧠 Use stream only if:
no index
no break/continue
just action

2️⃣ Filtering (if condition)
Loop
List<Integer> evens = new ArrayList<>();
for (int x : list) {
    if (x % 2 == 0) {
        evens.add(x);
    }
}

Stream
List<Integer> evens =
    list.stream()
        .filter(x -> x % 2 == 0)
        .toList();

🧠 Pattern:
if → filter

3️⃣ Transformation (map)
Loop
List<Integer> squares = new ArrayList<>();
for (int x : list) {
    squares.add(x * x);
}

Stream
List<Integer> squares =
    list.stream()
        .map(x -> x * x)
        .toList();

🧠 Pattern:
modify value → map

4️⃣ Filter + Map together (very common)
Loop
List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
for (int x : list) {
    if (x > 10) {
        result.add(x * 2);
    }
}

Stream
List<Integer> result =
    list.stream()
        .filter(x -> x > 10)
        .map(x -> x * 2)
        .toList();

🧠 Order matters:
filter → map

5️⃣ Find first matching element
Loop
Integer found = null;
for (int x : list) {
    if (x > 10) {
        found = x;
        break;
    }
}

Stream
Optional<Integer> found =
    list.stream()
        .filter(x -> x > 10)
        .findFirst();

🧠 Stream advantage:
short-circuiting
no manual break

6️⃣ Any / All / None checks
Loop
boolean hasNegative = false;
for (int x : list) {
    if (x < 0) {
        hasNegative = true;
        break;
    }
}

Stream
boolean hasNegative =
    list.stream().anyMatch(x -> x < 0);

🧠 Mapping:
exists → anyMatch
all → allMatch
none → noneMatch

7️⃣ Counting elements
Loop
int count = 0;
for (int x : list) {
    if (x % 2 == 0) count++;
}

Stream
long count =
    list.stream()
        .filter(x -> x % 2 == 0)
        .count();

8️⃣ Frequency counting (VERY IMPORTANT)
Loop
Map<Character, Integer> freq = new HashMap<>();
for (char c : str.toCharArray()) {
    freq.put(c, freq.getOrDefault(c, 0) + 1);
}

Stream
Map<Character, Long> freq =
    str.chars()
       .mapToObj(c -> (char) c)
       .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
           c -> c,
           Collectors.counting()
       ));

🧠 Rule:
grouping + counting → groupingBy + counting

9️⃣ First non-repeating character (stream version)
Loop version (you know this)
for (Map.Entry<Character, Integer> e : freq.entrySet()) {
    if (e.getValue() == 1) {
        System.out.println(e.getKey());
        break;
    }
}

Stream
freq.entrySet().stream()
    .filter(e -> e.getValue() == 1)
    .map(Map.Entry::getKey)
    .findFirst()
    .ifPresent(System.out::println);

